"gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T12:28:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T12:29:59Z","body":"> While working on https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114279 I noticed that the sky reflections were more contrast-y and then thought of this issue. Looking at the MRP in master, it actually looks more like what you want.\n\nWell, it's not just what I want; there is a physically correct solution that I think we want to reproduce as closely as possible.\n\n> Fixed by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107902\n\nIndeed, it is now way better! I agree it's good enough now to close the issue.\n\nFor reference, this is what I'm seeing:\n\n| Before fix (TAR off) | Before fix (TAR on) | After fix (`master`) | Reference (blender cycles) |\n|--------|--------|--------|--------|\n| <img width=\"674\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e8e4712a-abbb-4416-b407-8bf9a802c23e\" /> | <img width=\"474\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/de47bf06-ca36-4d18-a6a1-6b172503c85d\" /> | <img width=\"436\" height=\"399\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e248314c-fbaf-4a7a-aa0d-7bca40b85352\" /> | <img width=\"422\" height=\"422\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ffd64d44-8a85-4599-8f07-52e6d89a90d9\" /> | \n\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3768098932/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3769605921","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108273#issuecomment-3769605921","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108273","id":3769605921,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gr58h","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T18:12:56Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T18:12:56Z","body":"> Well, it's not just what I want; there is a physically correct solution that I think we want to reproduce as closely as possible.\n\nRight. The weird thing is that the algorithm is the same between versions as we did a 1-to-1 port basically. But somehow the overall look changed a lot. \n\nIts clear that we were doing something in 4.5 and earlier that led to a huge amount of over-blurring, but I still don't understand what it was. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com